    "title": "Houston Open prize payouts for 2026 winner Gary Woodland, every golfer",
    "text": "Updated March 29, 2026, 7:10 p.m. ETWhat looked like it would be a head-to-head battle heading into Sunday's final round at the Texas Children's Houston Open wound up being a bit of a blowout.After leading by just one stroke following Saturday's third round, 41-year-old Gary Woodland wound up winning by five strokes over second-place Nicolai Højgaard, his first win on tour since the 2019 U.S. Open. The victory earned Woodland an invitation to the 2026 Masters tournament as well.Woodland scored a huge payday just 2.5 years after undergoing brain surgery. It's a massive victory for someone who has been through a lot of mental struggles as of late.The title earned him $1.782 million. Not bad, huh? But it's still not even 20% of the total $9.9 million purse available at the Houston Open. Here's what each golfer took home at the end of the day.LEADERBOARD: Full results from Texas Children's Houston OpenHouston Open purse, payoutsThe PGA Tour's Texas Children's Houston Open has a total purse of $9.9 million, with $1.782 million going to the winner. Here is how the payout for each position breaks down:1. Gary Woodland (-21) — $1,782,0002. Nicolai Hojgaard (-16) — $1,079,100T3. Johnny Keefer (-15) — $584,100T3. Min Woo Lee (-14) — $584,1005. Sam Stevens (-14) — $405,900T6. Jake Knapp (-13) — $322,987T6. Chris Gotterup (-13) — $322,987T6. Sudarshan Yellamaraju (-13) — $322,987T6. Jason Day (-13) — $322,987T10. Bronson Burgoon (-12) — $259,875T10. Sahith Theegala (-12) — $259,875T12. Adrien Dumont de Chassart (-11) — $220,275T12. Denny McCarthy (-11) — $220,275T14. Keith Mitchell (-10) — $170,775T14. Thorbjorn Olesen (-10) — $170,775T14. Pontus Nyholm (-10) — $170,775T14. Jhonattan Vegas (-10) — $170,775T14. Michael Thorbjornsen (-10) — $170,775T19. Max McGreevy (-9) — $136,125T19. Karl Vilips (-9) — $136,125T21. Sam Burns (-8) — $96,525T21. Harris English (-8) — $96,525T21. Aldrich Potgieter (-8) — $96,525T21. Alex Smalley (-8) — $96,525T21. Beau Hossler (-8) — 